1 | backend-critic | READ-ONLY REVIEW of PR 2779 on branch task/2768-hold-pairing. You are not a producer: no commits, no push, no gh pr review, no gh pr merge, no labels, no test writing. The harness pushes the branch it checks out, so any commit on a producer ref is a production incident. Permitted writes are a slash tmp worktree only. Record the PR head SHA at start and re-check at report; if it moved report BLOCKED with both SHAs. THE INVARIANT UNDER TEST, stated by the PR itself: keep the traveller authorisation if and only if the client still offers a retry on this row. Issue 2715 closed one direction, do not RETAIN a hold for a retry the client refuses to offer. This PR claims to close the mirror direction, do not VOID a hold when the client does still invite the press. THE QUESTION THAT MATTERS: is the invariant now actually two sided, or has one direction been fixed by breaking the other. Enumerate the upstream statuses and refusal shapes the handler can see, and for EACH one state what the server now does with the hold and what the client does with the CTA, then say whether they agree. Read the client classifier yourself, apps/web/lib/checkout-failure.ts, rather than trusting the PR body about what the client offers, because the whole defect class here is the server and the client disagreeing about whether a retry exists. Pay particular attention to 401, 403, 429 and 5xx, which issue 2768 names, and to 409, which issue 2715 was about, and confirm the two fixes have not overlapped into a contradiction on any shared status. SECOND, the money direction matters more than symmetry. A wrongly VOIDED hold under a winner loses a booking the traveller thought they had; a wrongly RETAINED hold parks the traveller money until Stripe expiry with the orphan reaper worker PAUSED, which is the standing condition. Say explicitly which way each changed branch now errs and whether that is the safe direction for that branch. THIRD, verify by test rather than by reading: confirm the new tests in hold_retry_pairing_test.go and booking_order_timeout_test.go FAIL on the parent commit, reproducing that yourself in a throwaway worktree rather than accepting a claim, and that none of them passes trivially. FOURTH, confirm nothing in this diff changes whether a Stripe authorisation is CAPTURED, as opposed to voided or kept, since capture is a different irreversible action and is out of scope. FIFTH, check isRecoverableUserError specifically: issue 2715 and the earlier audit both traced defects to it classifying by HTTP status alone, so state whether this change makes that better, worse or unchanged. SIXTH, the PRD block in docs/prd/pages/07-checkout.md is marked PROPOSED pending co-founder sign-off and claims no new copy and no visible change. Verify that claim against the diff: any user visible string or behaviour change would mean the block needs sign-off before merge rather than after. Post ONE comment on issue 2340 whose first line reads CRITIC 2779 HOLD RETRY INVARIANT, with a verdict of SAFE-TO-MERGE or BLOCK-FIX or BLOCK-ESCALATE, per-finding severity and file and line citations. No vendor names, emails, booking ids or gcloud payloads. | task/2768-hold-pairing
